{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>He made him ride on the high places of the earth.</b> The entire verse is as its Targum renders." "<b>He made him ride, etc.</b> Because the land of Israel is higher than all the lands." "<b>And he ate the produce of the field.</b> These are the fruits of the land of Israel, which are quicker to bud and to ripen than all the fruits of the lands." "<b>And He suckled him with honey from the crag.</b> A story of one who said to his son in Sikhnin: Bring me fig-cakes from the barrel. He went and found honey floating on its mouth. He said to him: This one is of honey. He said to him: Plunge your hand into it and you will bring up fig-cakes from inside it (Sifrei)." "<b>High places of the earth.</b> A term of height." "<b>Shaddai.</b> A term of field." "<b>The flint of rock.</b> The might and strength of a rock: when it is not attached to the word after it, it is pointed חַלָּמִישׁ, and when it is attached, it is pointed חַלְמִישׁ." "<b>And oil from the flint of rock.</b> These are the olive trees of Gush Chalav (Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:17.097602539Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}